Two small input-handling slips in lib/MCP/K8s.pm:

1. `_build_namespaces` (line 358-360): `split /,/, $env` - `MCP_K8S_NAMESPACES="default, production"` yields the namespace `' production'`; its SelfSubjectRulesReview fails (warned), the namespace silently drops out of `allowed_namespaces`, and with one namespace left the tools start auto-filling `default`. Also an empty element from a trailing comma.
2. Tier-4 plural heuristic (line 465-468): `s/ys$/ies/` runs on every word, so a Kind ending in vowel+y is mangled: `Gateway` -> `gatewaies` (Kubernetes::REST's own heuristic in `_build_path` guards with `[^aeiou]y$`). Only reached when tiers 2 and 3 fail (CRD without class and no discovery rights), and then shows up as a misleading 'Permission denied' as CLAUDE.md already warns.

Done when: the list is split on `/\s*,\s*/` with empty entries dropped, the heuristic only rewrites consonant+y, both covered in t/02 and t/03.

